Subject: [PATCH] pandora: define IOAcceleratorES's meta class, the line 0333 was carrying

0184 declares the class with OSDeclareDefaultStructors only, which declares the meta
class but never defines it.  The definition lived in 0333, next to a registry sampler.
k354 dropped 0333 and the kernel stopped linking (IOAcceleratorES::gMetaClass undefined
from AGXAccelerator::MetaClass::MetaClass).  Keep the definition, leave the sampler out.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/PandoraAdrenoGpu.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/PandoraAdrenoGpu.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/PandoraAdrenoGpu.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/PandoraAdrenoGpu.cpp
@@ -594,6 +594,12 @@
 class IOAcceleratorES : public IOService {
 	OSDeclareDefaultStructors(IOAcceleratorES);
 };
 
+/*
+ * 0343: OSDeclareDefaultStructors leaves gMetaClass undefined, so AGXAccelerator cannot link
+ * without this one line.  0333 carried it next to a registry sampler that is not wanted here.
+ */
+OSDefineMetaClassAndStructors(IOAcceleratorES, IOService);
+
 class AGXAccelerator : public IOAcceleratorES {
 	OSDeclareDefaultStructors(AGXAccelerator);
